{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived","id":289425,"title":"Blog Post: Book of the Deceived","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-22T04:24:40-07:00","id":289425,"title":"Blog Post: Book of the Deceived","content":"Hi, guys!<br /> <br /> As a little thank you for your continued interest in <b>Mummy</b>, we've got a bit of a treat for you this time around, as you'll see in today's blog post...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/development-tease-the-deceived-mummy-the-curse/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/development-t...mmy-the-curse/</a><br /> <br /> CAS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T04:45:19-07:00","id":289442,"title":"","content":"Well, that's just beautiful.<br /> <br /> So we now know the Deceived definitely do use Pillars, and that they have Memory. My hopes that regular Mummies might be able to tap into the Will increase.<br /> <br /> As for the Dream-Eater him/itself, it makes for fascinating reading. The arrogant, wise, self-centred, soul devouring embodiment of music, touching reality through the immortal bodies of its servants and manifesting so strongly that they are almost entirely subsumed beneath the force of its power. I don't know what I was expecting with the Deceived, but it certainly wasn't something quite that interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T05:23:37-07:00","id":289452,"title":"","content":"Oh, very interesting. And it makes playing the Deceived look a very different experience than the regular Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T06:10:53-07:00","id":289484,"title":"","content":"Arisen, I regret to inform you that I am defecting to the other side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T06:27:38-07:00","id":289490,"title":"","content":"My evil plan to get a second gaming group together to run a game set in Jakarta to run concurrently with my current Mummy game is now in full swing. Occasional meet-ups and interactions with the existing Mummy players should provide hands-free boss fights. I already have players lined up. It shall be glorious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T06:41:45-07:00","id":289498,"title":"","content":"From looking at the names of the splats, I think we can assume that the Sixth Guild was a Guild of artists? (I don't if it was said already, I may have missed it).<br /> <br /> Also, notice that the First Wave claims to be the first to defy the &quot;voice of the empire, of its false gods&quot;. If it is literal, and that it references the Judges..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T06:46:11-07:00","id":289503,"title":"","content":"Father Scarab (if not one of the Temakh) and seba sound interesting. I think <b>DC</b> hinted that Deceived relics were true name words or 'concepts' so I'm wondering if seba refers to that.<br /> <br /> I half wondered how the Deceived manage to hide their culture from the Arisen but, you know...Memory. Plus all the Deceived share one of seven soul fragments, so presumably there's that which connects them all.<br /> <br /> Actually, do the Arisens' Memory block out recollection of the Deceived? <b>DC</b>, I think, hinted as well that the Judges just wipe whatever isn't relevant to their interests, hence why crossover matters so little to the average Mummy, but clearly the Arisen don't even believe the Sixth Guild exists anymore. So are the Judges wiping that Memory from them? That's scary, though I suppose it's in the Judges' best interests since the Deceived seem to know something their rivals don't","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T07:14:16-07:00","id":289561,"title":"","content":"Every time I hear something new about Mummy I love it a little bit more. Despite not playing or even running a real game (<i>Eve of Judgment</i> once doesn't count) I think it might be my favorite WoD game by now.<br /> <br /> The Temakh are shaping up to be one of my favorite elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T07:21:47-07:00","id":289566,"title":"","content":"Is the difference between the First Wave and the Singer the difference between Tuomas Holpainen and whoever he has as the singer of Nightwish at the time(Currently Floor)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T07:26:06-07:00","id":289568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=289566#post289566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the difference between the First Wave and the Singer the difference between Tuomas Holpainen and whoever he has as the singer of Nightwish at the time(Currently Floor)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seens the First Wave is more about Music from instruments, the Singer about singing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T07:36:26-07:00","id":289573,"title":"","content":"There's so much awesome in here. <br /> <br /> Conceptually, it makes sense that the Sixth Guild would focus on art and inspiration, given the very material focuses of the other Guilds. It makes it seem like the Sixth Guild was almost the heart and soul of the Nameless Empire, investing it with meaning.<br /> <br /> I LOVE how much personality the Temakh seem to have, especially compared to the Judges, who aren't really fleshed out all that much (presumably because Arisen don't really interact with the Judges until they Descend). The Temakh really come across as characters in their own rights, to the point that it's surprising to see the apparent antipathy between factions in the Deceived (the Dream-Eater seems to REALLY not like the Philosopher).<br /> <br /> Man, the hints in here about what was really going on in the Nameless Empire, and why the Sixth Guild was cast down, are intriguing. It looks to me like the Shan'iatu leading the Five Guilds conspired to set up the Judges in place of the existing gods of Duat, possibly with the promise of being able to live forever themselves in the afterlife, and that the Shan'iatu of the Sixth Guild had a real problem with that (except maybe for the Philosopher). Fascinating call-backs to Mage, if that's true!<br /> <br /> I see vague homages to Changeling in here as well. The mummies of the Dream-Eater appear to want to foster true inspiration, and then consume the fruits of that inspiration such that the world loses out on a potentially great work of art (presumably the Dream-Eater consumes the inspiration as sustenance or something). That's awfully dark. It gives the Deceived a nice bite; I'm glad that they apparently are themselves monstrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T07:36:49-07:00","id":289574,"title":"","content":"Close enough.<br /> <br /> But seriously, where have the Deceived been all my life?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Quick, someone develop a sax playing mummy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You know, I realize sometimes it seems like I reference Madoka a lot? I probably do. That said!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://38.media.tumblr.com/39c76c9c4134e3e53ad0df702db737f7/tumblr_n38462nrBw1r30su4o5_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I think I can be forgiven for this reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-22-2014, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T09:02:01-07:00","id":289639,"title":"","content":"I like how the Temakh, at least this one but hopefully all of them, have a mechanic that lets them feed off of humans somehow. Every splat has a way to do so (except <b>Promethean</b>?) and <b>Mummy</b> was lacking, other than Shuankhsen or the vague Sybaritic magic of cult formation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T09:11:51-07:00","id":289651,"title":"","content":"The more I read this, the more it seems like the Deceived really are bastards. Normal Arisen earn Sebayt experience through performing acts of great morality and learning about their past. Deceived (at least this version) apparently earn it as a result of turning humans into Willpower batteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T12:01:28-07:00","id":289839,"title":"","content":"Seba means &quot;star&quot;, according to the best source of all, google. Which makes perfect sense in light of the depiction of the Lost Guild as per Cursed Necropolis: DC.<br /> <br /> I *hope* that the Deceived are, well, bastards. The good thing about the antagonist factions of the WoD is that they're NOT protagonists who happen to have a different point of view. The Pure aren't misunderstood good guys. The Seers of the Throne aren't mages who simply have a different paradigm than members of the Pentacle. They're bad guys.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T12:05:03-07:00","id":289844,"title":"","content":"Also, yes, more importantly:<br /> <br /> Thanks for the spoilers, Colin! It is appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T12:36:17-07:00","id":289881,"title":"","content":"Thoughts:<br /> <br /> &quot;Misbegotten chorus of the Five&quot; - a reference to the lies of the other guilds?<br /> <br /> The Deceived of the philosopher are described as being somehow different from the others - &quot;the damned philosopher&quot;.<br /> <br /> What's left of the Shan'iatu really doesn't seem to be particularly nice or sane. I approve.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the cults of the Deceived is to &quot;deceive the Judges' get&quot;?<br /> <br /> Father Scarab?<br /> <br /> Seba (star) appears to be some sort of source of power for the Lost Guild.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T12:50:49-07:00","id":289893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=289881#post289881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts:<br /> <br /> &quot;Misbegotten chorus of the Five&quot; - a reference to the lies of the other guilds?<br /> <br /> The Deceived of the philosopher are described as being somehow different from the others - &quot;the damned philosopher&quot;.<br /> <br /> What's left of the Shan'iatu really doesn't seem to be particularly nice or sane. I approve.<br /> <br /> The purpose of the cults of the Deceived is to &quot;deceive the Judges' get&quot;?<br /> <br /> Father Scarab?<br /> <br /> Seba (star) appears to be some sort of source of power for the Lost Guild.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Misbegotten chorus of the Five&quot; - That's how I read it as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;Father Scarab&quot; - I read this as being an alternate name for the Temakh called the Keeper. Obviously could be wrong on that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T12:54:29-07:00","id":289899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=289839#post289839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seba means &quot;star&quot;, according to the best source of all, google. Which makes perfect sense in light of the depiction of the Lost Guild as per Cursed Necropolis: DC.<br /> <br /> I *hope* that the Deceived are, well, bastards. The good thing about the antagonist factions of the WoD is that they're NOT protagonists who happen to have a different point of view. The Pure aren't misunderstood good guys. The Seers of the Throne aren't mages who simply have a different paradigm than members of the Pentacle. They're bad guys.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd figured up until this point that the Shuankhsen filled that role. Not that I have any problem with the Deceived being monsters, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T13:58:07-07:00","id":289990,"title":"","content":"The Deceived are bastards with buy-in for Iremite culture and history.<br /> <br /> Shuankhsen are chattel slaves dragged in from elsewhere with no emotional investment in the enterprise except to see it all burn down (or get fed to a demonic oblivion goddess, whichever).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T14:27:23-07:00","id":290004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=289893#post289893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Father Scarab&quot; -- I read this as being an alternate name for the Temakh called the Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.troll.me