"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T04:46:23-07:00","id":290417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=289839#post289839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I *hope* that the Deceived are, well, bastards. The good thing about the antagonist factions of the WoD is that they're NOT protagonists who happen to have a different point of view. The Pure aren't misunderstood good guys. The Seers of the Throne aren't mages who simply have a different paradigm than members of the Pentacle. They're bad guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with Christian on this one. The Deceived need to be pretty demonstrable, its not like the Arisen are saints as it is. Hell, arguably the only &quot;good guy&quot; in the whole Mummy getting is the Heretic and even the forces of the divine he seems wrapped up with (the nameless gods) are at least a little dodgy. <br /> <br /> As for the Book of Going Westward, IF it happens (and its a big IF I feel) then its not going to be in the first 8-9 months of 2015 from the release schedule we have. Considering I expect Rio, Sothis, Dark Eras and Dreams to take at least another 9 months to a year to all come out (the only Mummy book I expect out this year besides Deceived is the Fiction Anthology - Curse of the Blue Nile), that's not really surprising.<br /> <br /> I imagine they (as in Onyx Path) would want to tally the results of the line once all its current books are out, then decide if they want to do more (like they did with Swords at Dawn and Dancers in the Dusk for Changeling) or just let the line rest until 2nd Edition in 2017.<br /> <br /> All this thought experiment rambling on my part is with an eye that we won't have the rest of the Mummy books for another year or so and that the devs start working on 2nd ed sometime in 2016 (much like Matt has been working on Promethean 2nd ed for ages before it got announced). So that might leave a descent gap of around 6-8 months where something could get developed. <br /> <br /> As always, just my 2p.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T05:51:39-07:00","id":290457,"title":"","content":"I just want to say I always get a little excited when I see Hawthorn post because he's always going to rein in with some wall of text &lt;3<br /> <br /> But I agree wholeheartedly this time. I'm sure the Deceived are compelling protagonists, but I want the majority of <b>Mummy</b> players to still mostly want to play regular Arisen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T15:07:24-07:00","id":290811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=290457#post290457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say I always get a little excited when I see Hawthorn post because he's always going to rein in with some wall of text &lt;3</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh reseru, you say the nicest things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly I'm amazed with the general grump I am on the Mummy forums that anyone could look forward to one of my posts.<br /> <br /> I'm the dour pessimist of the board that occasionally shouts out things that equate the forum equivalent of <i>&quot;the end is nigh&quot;</i> or <i>&quot;all is lost&quot;</i>. <br /> <br /> Anyway, back on topic, yes the Arisen should remain firmly planted as the protagonists of the game. The Deceived should be a nice well rounded option for when you feel like playing something with a different tone.<br /> <br /> Kinda like a Vampire game where you are playing Brood or a Mage game where you are playing Seers. Its fun, but its a whole different type of fun from the &quot;normal&quot; protagonists of the given line and allows you to tell slightly different stories with semi-familiar (yet twisted) trappings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T16:02:22-07:00","id":290835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=290811#post290811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh reseru, you say the nicest things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly I'm amazed with the general grump I am on the Mummy forums that anyone could look forward to one of my posts.<br /> <br /> I'm the dour pessimist of the board that occasionally shouts out things that equate the forum equivalent of <i>&quot;the end is nigh&quot;</i> or <i>&quot;all is lost&quot;</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but...that's <i>why</i> I look forward to your posts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T19:35:30-07:00","id":290956,"title":"","content":"So does anyone have the horrible feeling that <i>these</i> are the guys who developed Utterances and actually know the full sentences?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T20:11:14-07:00","id":290967,"title":"","content":"It was heavily implied in the Scribe's section of Guildhalls actually. I've been excited so I've been going over the 'known' facts of Deceived.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They are supposedly all Serpent-Headed/Ren Decree</li> <li>They were the cultural heart of the Irem.</li> <li>They are the 'masters of Nomenclature', name magic.</li> <li>They rebelled before the Rite of Return was performed.</li> <li>They are heretics.</li> <li>They are linked to Apotheosis.</li> <li>Their favoured relics are ephemeral, ideas, or concepts.</li> </ol>Did I miss anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 10-23-2014, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T20:38:55-07:00","id":290980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=290811#post290811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, back on topic, yes the Arisen should remain firmly planted as the protagonists of the game. The Deceived should be a nice well rounded option for when you feel like playing something with a different tone.<br /> <br /> Kinda like a Vampire game where you are playing Brood or a Mage game where you are playing Seers. Its fun, but its a whole different type of fun from the &quot;normal&quot; protagonists of the given line and allows you to tell slightly different stories with semi-familiar (yet twisted) trappings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one thing that sets them apart from utter bastards like the Seers is that there will be an element of tragedy to the Deceived that may make them relatable. Everyone gets screwed over by the dread stratagems of Duat - Arisen, Shuankhsen, and even the mortal members of the Scorpion Cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T21:17:24-07:00","id":290996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=290967#post290967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was heavily implied in the Scribe's section of Guildhalls actually. I've been excited so I've been going over the 'known' facts of Deceived.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>They are supposedly all Serpent-Headed/Ren Decree</li> <li>They were the cultural heart of the Irem.</li> <li>They are the 'masters of Nomenclature', name magic.</li> <li>They rebelled before the Rite of Return was performed.</li> <li>They are heretics.</li> <li>They are linked to Apotheosis.</li> <li>Their favoured relics are ephemeral, ideas, or concepts.</li> </ol>Did I miss anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only one I can think of to add is that Name Magic is supposedly based on Will-Working. The Sesha-Hebsu claim that magic has two halves, the Word and the Will. Utterances are the Word, rote magic, and the only magic the five Guilds were ever allowed to learn. It's speculated that the reason the Deceived had to be destroyed was because they were keepers of the Will, and thus had a far greater grasp of what magic was and what their masters were doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T22:32:17-07:00","id":291063,"title":"","content":"There's a connection between the Lost Guild and stars, the night sky, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T06:19:15-07:00","id":291252,"title":"","content":"Random thoughts on the Deceived, based on what we (think we) know:<br /> <br /> It seems clear from the First Wave's description that the Shan'iatu of the Sixth Guild were not on-board with the Judges for some reason (see the talk about deceiving the Judges' get, etc.) I think this is supported by the idea that the Deceived are often described as heretics. That term is also used to describe the one Arisen who has achieved Apotheosis thus far, a process which severs the hold of the Judge over the Arisen. Since normal Arisen existence is based on serving the will of the Judges, and the Judges are considered to be divine, cutting ties to them or opposing them is considered heretical. It seems to me like the Judges were a controversial topic in the Nameless Empire. <br /> <br /> If that's true, I think I'd actually prefer it if the status of the Deceived as a benign or malevolent faction is left ambiguous and in the hands of the Storyteller, depending on how each Storyteller wants to treat the &quot;truth&quot; of the Judges. Maybe the Judges really are divine and their mandates axiomatically just (no matter how harsh that seems to us), and the Deceived truly are in the wrong for opposing them (which lends an interesting twist to Apotheosis). Or maybe the Judges were usurpers of the natural order in some sense, and the Deceived have a point. <br /> <br /> I like that ambiguity more than simply making the Deceived similar to the Seers of the Throne, who are pretty objectively rotten to the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:08:28-07:00","id":291481,"title":"","content":"My problem with moral ambiguity is that ambiguity makes people want to play Deceived. And that makes playing the Arisen, the core protagonists of the game, less attractive, which is all kinds of problematic.<br /> <br /> It's like the old fera problem in Werewolf: the Apocalypse. Present the fera as playable options and suddenly noone wants to play werewolves. The core concept of the game is diluted, resulting in a less coherent game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:21:29-07:00","id":291488,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean ambiguous in the same way that the Technocracy was ambiguous starting in Mage 2E. Assuming everything else I put in that post, what I meant was that it'd be nice if the truth of the Judges, the question of whether it's a good thing to serve them or not (and therefore whether the Arisen are dupes or the Deceived are double-dyed monsters), is left up to the individual Storyteller, with no real &quot;default&quot; answer. It makes even Apotheosis potentially problematic, which I rather like. <br /> <br /> For me, it avoids the Seers problem. Even though the Seers ARE playable, doing so feels pretty disgusting because they're so objectively awful. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:36:17-07:00","id":291579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=291481#post291481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with moral ambiguity is that ambiguity makes people want to play Deceived. And that makes playing the Arisen, the core protagonists of the game, less attractive, which is all kinds of problematic.<br /> <br /> It's like the old fera problem in Werewolf: the Apocalypse. Present the fera as playable options and suddenly noone wants to play werewolves. The core concept of the game is diluted, resulting in a less coherent game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, part of the problem is ...well,the devs do want the Deceived to be playable. So, the grand ol question is &quot;How do I make this thing desirable without overshadowing the thing I already have?&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the fact that the Deceived risk loss of individuality to their Temakhs will go a long way with that, but for now I say wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T14:49:35-07:00","id":291586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=291579#post291579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, part of the problem is ...well,the devs do want the Deceived to be playable. So, the grand ol question is &quot;How do I make this thing desirable without overshadowing the thing I already have?&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the fact that the Deceived risk loss of individuality to their Temakhs will go a long way with that, but for now I say wait and see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Deceived will be playable, but I don't think they'll overshadow the Arisen since the Arisen are closer to what we think of as the classic pulp Mummy experience. They rise to pursue tomb robbers and exact deadly vengeance with horrific miracles. There's some flexibility with the Deceived that allows them to diverge from that narrative by doing stuff like attending rock concerts and devouring inspiration. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T15:00:23-07:00","id":291591,"title":"","content":"See, the current problem with the Deceived is the sensation that they are freed from the same constraint as the Arisen. Certainly they'll face some sort of conflict, but that hasn't been made apparent to us. For now, we know they do not exist fully within the same set of lies and demands the other five guilds face-they stand outside and they know 'better'. The trade-off has been the repeated implication that they are <i>non compos mentis, </i>which as the Masquerade players will tell you tends to actually be a draw for a fair number of the audience.<br /> <br /> Wait and see-we'll see their catch soon enough. (Who am I talking to? No idea)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T16:31:11-07:00","id":291616,"title":"","content":"Well, Octavo, I think the Deceived are still bound to certain magicks. They <i>are</i> still Mummies after all, with the legacy of the Nameless Empire bound into their bones whether they like it or not. Perhaps they weren't created by the Rite of Return as the Arisen, or as a pre-requisite for the Rite as the Shuankhsen sacrifices were, but they still have the Memory trait and I suspect their awakenings are still tied to Sothic turns as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=291579#post291579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the fact that the Deceived risk loss of individuality to their Temakhs will go a long way with that, but for now I say wait and see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is an interesting revelation. There's the horror most likely right there: the Arisen lose themselves to the Judges' service, but the Deceived have lost themselves to being 'possessed' by these broken soul-fragments of a Shan'iatu. They have to build up Memory to remember that, &quot;Oh shit, I used to be a person that cared about things. Why do I let this divine sorcerer spirit take over my actions and thoughts?&quot;<br /> <br /> I like it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T16:38:22-07:00","id":291617,"title":"","content":"Let's not call it a revelation-makes it sound like I know things others don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T16:59:36-07:00","id":291628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=291586#post291586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Deceived will be playable, but I don't think they'll overshadow the Arisen since the Arisen are closer to what we think of as the classic pulp Mummy experience. They rise to pursue tomb robbers and exact deadly vengeance with horrific miracles. There's some flexibility with the Deceived that allows them to diverge from that narrative by doing stuff like attending rock concerts and devouring inspiration. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well maybe the Deceived unlike the Arisen cannot seek Apotheosis, so the &quot;redemption&quot; angle wouldn't apply to them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T17:35:27-07:00","id":291655,"title":"","content":"That's a good point, too. We keep thinking that they have hints of connections to Apotheosis, but can they even break the bonds of their Temakh? The Arisen can break their chains from the Judges (ahem...theoretically), but the Temakh are filling in a Deceived's cracked soul like a cavity filling it seems. How can you break that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T17:41:54-07:00","id":291680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=291655#post291655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point, too. We keep thinking that they have hints of connections to Apotheosis, but can they even break the bonds of their Temakh? The Arisen can break their chains from the Judges (ahem...theoretically), but the Temakh are filling in a Deceived's cracked soul like a cavity filling it seems. How can you break that?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be even more tragic if they have all the information on Apotheosis(they seen to be closer to the 5 Nameless Gods) but not able to act on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 10-24-2014, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T06:23:49-07:00","id":293689,"title":"","content":"No matter how the Deceived turn out, I definitely think there's still room for the Arisen to shine, especially as heroes (by comparison). For example, one of the big &quot;things&quot; the Arisen do is effectively remove relics from the world. Given how problematic relics can be (see, e.g., the effigy that drives people insane just by looking at it), that's actually a pretty good activity in which to engage. The fewer monkey paws floating around, the better. Compare to the mummies of the Dream-Eater, who remove inspiration from the world. A fairly awful thing to do.<br /> <br /> All that being said, I can't wait for the book! Starting this Wednesday, I'll be visiting DriveThruRPG a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","user":"Brian888","date":". 10-27-2014, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T08:08:42-07:00","id":293732,"title":"","content":"We are nowhere near that three week mark. Again, hold off unless we get something new that says otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:15:17-07:00","id":293858,"title":"","content":"Just to back-up Arcane again. Its really not worth getting excited over a possible release until at least after the Monday Morning notes are out for this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:25:05-07:00","id":294083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=293689#post293689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter how the Deceived turn out, I definitely think there's still room for the Arisen to shine, especially as heroes (by comparison). For example, one of the big &quot;things&quot; the Arisen do is effectively remove relics from the world. Given how problematic relics can be (see, e.g., the effigy that drives people insane just by looking at it), that's actually a pretty good activity in which to engage. The fewer monkey paws floating around, the better. Compare to the mummies of the Dream-Eater, who remove inspiration from the world. A fairly awful thing to do.<br /> <br /> All that being said, I can't wait for the book! Starting this Wednesday, I'll be visiting DriveThruRPG a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I'm mistaken, don't the relics appear mysteriously elsewhere sometimes after they've been sent to Duat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:37:06-07:00","id":294092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=294083#post294083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless I'm mistaken, don't the relics appear mysteriously elsewhere sometimes after they've been sent to Duat?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanism by which relics occasionally return to the mortal sphere appears to be decidedly less common than the supernatural-bomb-defusing that the Arisen regularly engage in, if I remember the allusion correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T18:54:53-07:00","id":294403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=294092#post294092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanism by which relics occasionally return to the mortal sphere appears to be decidedly less common than the supernatural-bomb-defusing that the Arisen regularly engage in, if I remember the allusion correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T19:03:14-07:00","id":294409,"title":"","content":"The Judges only appear to return relics to the world when doing so could net them a tangible advantage, one greater than that lost by giving up the Sekhem invested in the relic in question. As Satchel says, that makes it a fairly unusual occurrence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T19:26:02-07:00","id":294423,"title":"","content":"And today's Meeting confirms what I've been saying,as the artwork is still being worked on.<br /> <br /> T'would have been nice for it to come out this week, but we still got a bit to go. Keep on keeping on guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T21:48:58-07:00","id":294519,"title":"","content":"I'm going to make a foolish prediction that it will come out the Wed after Halloween.<br /> #SybariticVisions<br /> #OkReallyWhiskeyVisions<br /> <