"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T06:07:36-07:00","id":294741,"title":"","content":"It seens nearly finished tough, just some art missing that will get in by the end of the week. And if I'm not mistaken they will realese it as a PDF first for fan errata, so should be relatively quick, but it won't happen this week I'm afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T14:19:00-07:00","id":295232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=294729#post294729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">la la la I'm still waiting on the edge of my seat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously. I'm jonesing hard for this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T16:50:35-07:00","id":295381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=294729#post294729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">la la la I'm still waiting on the edge of my seat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you!!<br /> I will probably be very satisfied when I get my hands on Deceived, but fully aware that it won't be long until I clamor for Sothis as well<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I want my Mummy!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T17:27:54-07:00","id":295416,"title":"","content":"I'm actually more excited for <b>Dark Eras</b> than <b>Book of the Deceived</b>! And while I hope to play through some flashbacks in Sothic periods, I probably wouldn't make heavy use of <b>Sothis Ascends</b> until my theoretical second campaign, where the PCs play through each Sothic turn in succession","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T17:56:42-07:00","id":295460,"title":"","content":"I'm the opposite. Of the entire line-up, Deceived is the one I've most been looking forward to. Sothis Ascends and Dark Eras are each going to be detailing historical periods, and while it'll be fascinating to see the writers' takes on them and how Arisen slot in, it's something you can more or less work out for yourself with a bit of research. The Deceived, on the other hand, are very nearly unusable as anything more than background villains, and even then you can only really guess at what their objectives could be. They're one of the line's principle antagonists, and yet they're close to impossible to use.<br /> <br /> Even if I weren't planning on running a Deceived game to compliment my current Mummy campaign, I'd be more interested to see what is in Deceived than the other books. The rest offer to expand on what we already have. Deceived offers something new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 10-28-2014, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T19:39:10-07:00","id":295533,"title":"","content":"Sothis Ascends isn't likely to get much mileage out of me, I'm afraid, unless there's something in it beyond the Turns themselves. Dark Eras seems super neat, but would superer neater if it were a WW2 North Africa setting or deacribed ethnic conflicts in the Middle East.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T19:59:27-07:00","id":295555,"title":"","content":"I don't discriminate between awesome.<br /> <br /> That said, Deceived is staring me in the face, Ascends is still a ways off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T05:22:57-07:00","id":295727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=295460#post295460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're one of the line's principle antagonists, and yet they're close to impossible to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey I can't argue with that, but <i>personally </i>- regardless of what the line needs at the moment - <b>Mummy</b> in its <b>Dark Era</b> is the whole inspiration behind my game:<br /> <br /> &quot;What if we got to see the movies from Imhotep's perspective?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, to a degree you did. We just missed out on the part where other mummies wake up and try to eat his flesh so they can be sacrificed to the lower-case-abyss","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T06:16:52-07:00","id":295789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=295533#post295533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sothis Ascends isn't likely to get much mileage out of me, I'm afraid, unless there's something in it beyond the Turns themselves. Dark Eras seems super neat, but would superer neater if it were a WW2 North Africa setting or deacribed ethnic conflicts in the Middle East.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hum, I have the growing suspicion that Sothis will also be about Apotheosis(after all is during a Sothic Turn that the Arisen awaken without a purpose, free to do whatever they want)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T06:27:28-07:00","id":297050,"title":"","content":"The descriptions of most of the other temakhs seem pretty self-explanatory (the Painter, the Dancer, etc.) However, I wonder what the Keeper is supposed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T23:21:40-07:00","id":297857,"title":"","content":"My guess would be a collector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T10:56:44-08:00","id":301302,"title":"","content":"A collector of what, though? Oh well, I guess we'll find out soon enough. I have a good feeling about this week!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attach