te.edu/images/filecabinet/folder4/resize/24/200x200.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Maaaaybe.<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, Thorn is right, on both counts.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To be fair I miss most of your references, just that XXXholic is one of those series that sticks in ones mind (through sheer awesome). Though I always viewed it as more of a source of Changeling or Mage inspiration then Mummy (well expect the Monkey Paw episode, that has &quot;Human interacting with a powerful relic&quot; written all over it). <br /> <br /> Looking back on the first page of this thread, totally can't believe I did not get the Madoka reference before you posted the gif. <br /> <br /> Anyway...this is totally not off-topic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:04:36-08:00","id":302272,"title":"","content":"I only made the one Madoka reference with the gif, and to be fair I was hoping people would get it as a grand supernatural act of music without knowing the context.<br /> <br /> How many references do I ma-off topic.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Holic is a good Werewolf and Geist inspiration due to it's interactions with the ethereal. In a vicarious way, that also makes it good for Mummy since the Arisen have an underscore of dealing with the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:24:32-08:00","id":302308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=302272#post302272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Holic is a good Werewolf and Geist inspiration due to it's interactions with the ethereal. In a vicarious way, that also makes it good for Mummy since the Arisen have an underscore of dealing with the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I never thought about that aspect. I always viewed the monsterious/mythic &quot;otherworld&quot; elements as more Changelingy then Werewolfy. Geist I can see now you point it out certainly. <br /> <br /> Actually Yuuko does seem to have a magical space (like a tomb) full of old powerful magic items (sorta like relics and vestiges) and often has to deal with problematic magic (like curses). She's also often complaining about being tired...so some Mummy inspirations to draw from there. Though depending on how the info in BotD she might be less Arisen and more Deceived in nature...<br /> <br /> Anyway, totally not continuing to be off topic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:31:36-08:00","id":302354,"title":"","content":"I don't know how much longer I can live without this book. But continue the anime references, by all means!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:36:07-08:00","id":302361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=302354#post302354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how much longer I can live without this book. But continue the anime references, by all means!</div> </div> </div> </div>Tomorrow I will be visiting drivethrurpg in a unhealthy frequency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:42:37-08:00","id":302373,"title":"","content":"Holic in general is kind of a grab bag for the whole World of Darkness. Yuuko herself fits in as a Mage, a fae, a ghost, a mummy, etc. The spirits and ghosts can be construed in any number of ways, from the afore mentioned to fae to infernal demons to supernal and astral entitites-often within the same creature. It's flexible and doesn't offer answers easily, fitting into the toolbox mystery nature of the setting beautifully.<br /> <br /> If I ever get around to finishing it(I know spoilers, no fear), I might just declare it one of the perfect sources for WoD period.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> So prior to finding out about the Temakhs, I had been devising a character for Idigam, a girl who's played it safe her entire life, but with the first change has started to try sloughing that off, including pursuing her desire to be a DJ. I dunno if I could get a group who could do a whole music theme thing, but that was in my head.<br /> <br /> Then we found out about the Temakhs, and now I want a battle between a scrappy electronic music pack up against a Deceived performance hall. Classic and more established music against the chaotic experimentality and less validated of the younger genres, an allegory I suppose.<br /> <br /> I also want an excuse to play Les Friction's Louder Than Words, but it doesn't have to be in that context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-04-2014, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:19:35-08:00","id":302426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/289425-blog-post-book-of-the-deceived?p=302373#post302373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holic in general is kind of a grab bag for the whole World of Darkness. Yuuko herself fits in as a Mage, a fae, a ghost, a mummy, etc. The spirits and ghosts can be construed in any number of ways, from the afore mentioned to fae to infernal demons to supernal and astral entitites-often within the same creature. It's flexible and doesn't offer answers easily, fitting into the toolbox mystery nature of the setting beautifully.<br /> <br /> If I ever get around to finishing it(I know spoilers, no fear), I might just declare it one of the perfect sources for WoD period.<br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> So prior to finding out about the Temakhs, I had been devising a character for Idigam, a girl who's played it safe her entire life, but with the first change has started to try sloughing that off, including pursuing her desire to be a DJ. I dunno if I could get a group who could do a whole music theme thing, but that was in my head.<br /> <br /> Then we found out about the Temakhs, and now I want a battle between a scrappy electronic group up against a Deceived performance hall.<br /> <br /> I also want an excuse to play Les Friction's Louder Than Words, but it doesn't have to be in that context.</div> </div> </div> </div>I pretty much agree with you about XXXholic being a bit of a one stop shop for inspirational stuff for the NWoD. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of having a &quot;scrappy&quot; coalition of Werewolves, Changelings and Geists vs a stuffy music group under the thumb of the Deceived and some Kindred. I believe this wonders into the &quot;Autobots Rock Out!&quot; trope a fair bit.<br /> <br /> You need an excuse to play Les Friction? Just listen to the damn thing on loop, I find it makes the day 100% more epic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T12:17:43-08:00","id":302526,"title":"","content":"It's a matter of playing it within context of the game.<br /> <br /> As for the music culture clash, what can I say? Who doesn't love a good epic final fight? Who doesn't love a battle of the bands? Only way things can get better is to mix the two together than the throw in some powers from beyond to boot.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, this is why the First Wave, the Singer, and the Dancer all appeal to me hardcore. I mean, I love the other Temakhs? but I'm defecting to the Deceived for those guys., even if I can't contribute to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:24:03-08:00","id":302691,"title":"","content":"Interesting point of view Arts.<br /> <br /> See I like what's mentioned about the Temakhs due to the tease for several other ones not really dwelt on in the previews.<br /> <br /> Being a bit of a musical dunce and lacking any motivation towards anything resembling &quot;dancing&quot; these guys are interesting, but I'm pretty sure a lot of their nuance is going to go over my head.<br /> <br /> I'm defecting to the Deceived for the Keeper and the Philosopher, because I like me some social-science and occultism wherever I can get it. Particularly when the two are mixed together and given a good healthy dose of oddness on top of all that. <br /> <br /> The Scribes and the Priests have kinda been covering those bases for me in Mummy (with a little bit of help from the Father of Idols). Really though, from the teased stuff they sound like groups that might end up joining Y-splats like the Ordo Dracul, Argentum Refinement and Inquisitor Agenda as one of my all time favorite social splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:58:13-08:00","id":302710,"title":"","content":"I hear you on all of that, and I do want to clarify that the other excite me as well as a psuedo-social-scientist and casual occultist researcher. Really, I love all of these guys. for reasons previously stated alone.(Liberal Arts Majors are my peeps)<br /> <br /> But those three-man, music is for me what water is to a fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T17:42:01-08:00","id":302785,"title":"","content":"So, I read Monday Meeting's comments?<br /> <br /> Rich pretty much all but confirmed that it's out tomorrow.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't come out tomorrow, you can point your scorn at me, but I'm fairly convinced that won't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T18:01:21-08:00","id":302796,"title":"","content":"I'm actually on the fence about those SOOOOON comments, but here's hopin'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T18:16:43-08:00","id":302807,"title":"","content":"I'm going to blindly believe.<br /> <br /> And probably leads scores of us to despair as a result.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's really late, but Thorn, the short hand name is Arc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-04-2014, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","va